Process a single bootstrap sample for Gate Set Tomography. This function performs a GST analysis on a sampled dataset, applies gauge optimization,
and generates result reports. y_sampled ( ndarray ) – A 2D array of measurement outcomes for sequences in J;
Each column contains the outcome probabilities for a fixed sequence attrs ( dict [ str , Any ] ) – Dictionary containing configuration parameters for the GST algorithm init ( list [ ndarray ] ) – Initial values for the gate set optimization [K, E, rho] target_model ( list [ ndarray ] ) – The target gate set model in format [X_target, E_target, rho_target] identifier ( str ) – String identifier for the current qubit layout X_opt_pp, array of optimized gate tensors in Pauli basis E_opt_pp, optimized POVM elements in Pauli basis rho_opt_pp, optimized initial state in Pauli basis df_g.values, array of gate quality measures df_o.values, array of SPAM and other quality measures Whether the optimization successfully converged below expected least-squares error. X_opt_pp, array of optimized gate tensors in Pauli basis E_opt_pp, optimized POVM elements in Pauli basis rho_opt_pp, optimized initial state in Pauli basis df_g.values, array of gate quality measures df_o.values, array of SPAM and other quality measures Whether the optimization successfully converged below expected least-squares error. tuple [ ndarray , ndarray , ndarray , ndarray , ndarray , bool ] previous iqm.benchmarks.compressive_gst.gst_analysis.pandas_results_to_observations next iqm.benchmarks.compressive_gst.gst_analysis.process_layout By IQM Benchmarks developers © Copyright 2024, IQM. Last updated on 2026-11-10.

Post processor to calculate and add three state probabilities to the dataset. Use readout average response phase settings and observations to compute the probabilities of three states,
using the barycentric coordinates method from raw complex readout. The processed data will have the shape (len(hard_sweeps[0]), ..., len(hard_sweeps[-1]), s0, s1, ...) ,
where s0, s1 etc. denote the dimensions of the soft sweeps. See compute_three_state_probability() for more details about the computation. run_result ( RunResult ) – The run result containing the full dataset and run data. qubit ( str ) – Qubit whose readout to classify. The RunResult object with GROUND_STATE_PROBABILITY , EXCITED_STATE_PROBABILITY and F_STATE_PROBABILITY added to the dataset. and F_STATE_PROBABILITY added to the dataset. list [ DataArray ] previous exa.core.multistate_classifier.utils.apply_assignment_inverse next exa.core.multistate_classifier.utils.get_assigment_inverse By Author name not set © Copyright 2019-2026, IQM Finland Oy, Release 20.0.0. Last updated on 2026-11-10.

